  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "When a positive integer \\(x\\) is divided by a positive integer \\(y,\\) the quotient is \\(u\\) and the remainder is \\(v,\\) where \\(u\\) and \\(v\\) are integers. What is the remainder when \\(x+2uy\\) is divided by \\(y?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(2u\\)",
    "C": "\\(3u\\)",
    "D": "\\(v\\)",
    "E": "\\(2v\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The given division means\n\\[\nx=uy+v,\\qquad 0\\le v<y.\n\\]\nSubstitute this into the new dividend:\n\\[\nx+2uy=uy+v+2uy=(3u)y+v.\n\\]\nThe added amount supplies whole multiples of \\(y\\). Since \\(3u\\) is an integer and \\(v\\) still satisfies \\(0\\le v<y\\), the new quotient is \\(3u\\) and the remainder is \\(\\boxed{v}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
